2️⃣ Docker Setup

Humne Docker use kiya.

Docker kya karta hai?

Simple example:

Normally hume manually install karna padta:

n8n
PostgreSQL
Node dependencies
configuration
etc.

Docker mein hum services ko containers mein run karte hain:

Docker
│
├── n8n Container
│
└── PostgreSQL Container

Har container isolated environment mein run hota hai.
Docker Start Karne Ki Koshish

Humne initially run kiya:

docker compose up -d
Iska matlab:

docker compose

→ Docker Compose ko use karo.

up

→ services create/start karo.

-d

→ detached mode; terminal ko block mat karo, background mein run karo.

Expected architecture:

docker compose up -d

       ↓

PostgreSQL starts
       +
n8n starts
7️⃣ Pehle Docker Error Aaya

Initially error tha:

failed to connect to the docker API
Meaning:

Docker command installed thi, lekin:

Docker Engine running nahi tha.

Isliye containers start nahi ho rahe the.

8️⃣ docker info

Humne run kiya:

docker info
Is command ka purpose?

Ye Docker Engine ki detailed information show karta hai.

Tumhare output mein:

Server Version: 29.4.2
Operating System: Docker Desktop
OSType: linux
Kernel Version: ... WSL2

aaya.

Isse confirm hua:

Docker Engine → Running ✅
9️⃣ docker run hello-world

Humne test ke liye:

docker run hello-world

chalaya.

Iska purpose?

Ye Docker ka basic health test hai.

Concept:

Docker
 ↓
hello-world image download
 ↓
container run
 ↓
Hello from Docker!

Agar ye successful ho:

Docker properly containers run kar sakta hai.

🔟 Docker Compose Start

Phir:

docker compose up -d

chalaya.

Is baar:

opspilot-postgres Healthy
opspilot-n8n Running

aaya.

Lekin baad mein status check karne par n8n:

Restarting (1)

nikla.

1️⃣1️⃣ docker compose ps

Humne command use ki:

docker compose ps
Iska purpose?

Ye batata hai ke Compose ke containers ki current state kya hai.

Example:

NAME
opspilot-n8n
opspilot-postgres

STATUS
Up
Healthy

Hamare case mein pehle:

n8n → Restarting ❌
PostgreSQL → Healthy ✅

tha.

1️⃣2️⃣ n8n Error Find Kiya

Humne run kiya:

docker compose logs n8n --tail=100
Iska matlab:

logs

→ container ke logs dikhao.

n8n

→ specifically n8n service.

--tail=100

→ last 100 log lines.

Error mila:

Error: Command "n8n" not found
1️⃣3️⃣ Root Cause Find Hua

Devin ne check karke discover kiya ke docker-compose.yml mein:

command: n8n start

tha.

Problem:

Official n8n Docker image already apna startup command provide karti hai.

Humne us command ko manually override kar diya tha.

Isliye n8n properly start nahi hua.

1️⃣4️⃣ Devin ne Fix Kiya

Ye remove kiya:

command: n8n start

Ab n8n image ka default startup command use hota hai.

Result:

n8n:

Up ✅
1️⃣5️⃣ Final Docker Restart

Humne:

docker compose down

use kiya.

down kya karta hai?

Current Compose containers ko stop/remove karta hai.

Simple:

Running containers
       ↓
docker compose down
       ↓
containers stopped/removed

Volumes normally remain karte hain, isliye persistent data preserve ho sakta hai.

Phir:

docker compose up -d

Dobara services start ki.

1️⃣6️⃣ Final Status

Latest result:

opspilot-n8n
STATUS: Up
PORT: 5678

opspilot-postgres
STATUS: Up (healthy)
PORT: 5432
Therefore:
Docker                 ✅
Docker Engine          ✅
Docker Compose         ✅
PostgreSQL             ✅
PostgreSQL Health      ✅
n8n                    ✅
n8n Port 5678          ✅
n8n Account            ✅
1️⃣7️⃣ n8n Account

Humne browser mein:

http://localhost:5678

open kiya.

n8n setup screen aayi.

Tumne account create kar liya.

Iska matlab:

Browser
   ↓
localhost:5678
   ↓
Docker
   ↓
n8n Container
   ↓
n8n UI

successfully working hai.

⚠️ Ek Warning Abhi Baqi Hai

Har Docker Compose command par:

the attribute `version` is obsolete

warning aa rahi hai.

Iska matlab?

docker-compose.yml mein old-style:

version: ...

field hai.

Ye error nahi hai.

Project chal raha hai.

Later professional cleanup mein isko remove karenge.

